--
Itanium C++ ABI 2.4 II.1 (g++/clang; N5008 leaves the layout of a dynamic
class to the implementation): a class shares its primary base's virtual
pointer -- its vtable struct embeds the primary base's as `@base' -- and the
primary base subobject is laid out first.  Before: `X : P' with new virtuals
was 24 bytes (own `@vtable_pointer'), and `S : R, P' kept declaration order.
The expected sizes and offsets are those of the LP64 x86_64 data model
(`--64'); the test is not meaningful in a 32-bit configuration.
